From ee3de3da7bb405b4eab2420f90341948e8fe8b80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix <52862870+devilAPI@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:58:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 35/38] iio: qcom_smgr: QMI length fields are u32 in the C
 structs

The QMI encoder and decoder copy a QMI_DATA_LEN value as a u32 from and
to the C struct (qmi_encdec.c), with elem_size giving the size on the
wire only. With u8 length fields the encoder read the next three bytes
too: a buffering request for any sensor other than ID 0 failed with
'qmi_encode: Invalid data length', so only the accelerometer could be
enabled. Make the length fields u32 and set the wire size to one byte
explicitly, as in other QMI users.

Tested on the ZTE Axon 7: accelerometer, gyroscope and magnetometer all
stream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FVN6i64chehV1XxwjxyaGp
